          {
            "pk": "fbc_bounds_v1/Model:fbc_bounds_v1",
            "sbmlType": "Model",
            "id": "fbc_bounds_v1",
            "metaId": "meta_fbc_bounds_v1",
            "name": "Flux bounds of fbc Version 1",
            "sbo": null,
            "notes": "<notes>\n  <body xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n    <p>Example of the first version of the fbc package, in which the capacity of a reaction is not an attribute of the reaction but a <code>fluxBound</code> object of its own.</p>\n    <p>Every bound names the reaction it constrains, the operation which relates the flux to its value and the value itself, so that two bounds are needed to keep a flux inside an interval and a third states an equality. The reaction <code>v1</code> carries such a pair, the exchange <code>EX_glc</code> is fixed by one bound of the operation <code>equal</code>, and the upper bound of <code>v1</code> is infinite, which is how the package writes an unbounded direction.</p>\n    <p>The model defines two objectives and declares the maximisation of the biomass as the active one; the second objective minimises the glucose uptake with a negative coefficient. The species carry the chemical formula and the charge which fbc adds to them in every one of its versions.</p>\n  </body>\n</notes>",
            "cvterms": [],
            "history": null,
